IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-unlawful-societies`

-- Societies Act 1966, ss 14 to 25 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures -- society status`

GIVEN `is a society` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `organised wholly outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `carries on activity in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an unapproved branch` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a triad ritual` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dissolution ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A SocietyStatus
DECIDE `a status` `is a society` `is registered` `organised wholly outside Singapore` `carries on activity in Singapore` `the Registrar is satisfied` `an unapproved branch` `uses a triad ritual` `dissolution ordered` IS
    SocietyStatus WITH
        `is a society within section 2` IS `is a society`
        `is a registered society` IS `is registered`
        `is organised wholly outside Singapore` IS `organised wholly outside Singapore`
        `carries on any activity in Singapore` IS `carries on activity in Singapore`
        `the Registrar is satisfied of both of those things` IS `the Registrar is satisfied`
        `is a branch established without the Registrar's prior approval` IS `an unapproved branch`
        `uses a triad ritual` IS `uses a triad ritual`
        `a dissolution order has been made against it under section 24` IS `dissolution ordered`

`a registered society in good standing` MEANS `a status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unregistered society` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unregistered group of nine` MEANS `a status` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unregistered society wholly abroad with no local activity and the Registrar satisfied` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the same, but the Registrar is not satisfied` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unregistered society organised abroad that carries on an activity here` MEANS `a status` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a registered society's unapproved branch` MEANS `a status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a registered society that uses a triad ritual` MEANS `a status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a registered society after a dissolution order` MEANS `a status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 14(1) and its cousins -- what makes a society unlawful`

#ASSERT NOT `the society is an unlawful society` `a registered society in good standing`

-- The default is the offence.
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `an unregistered society`
#ASSERT NOT `the society is an unlawful society` `an unregistered group of nine`

-- The foreign exemption needs wholly abroad, no activity here, AND the Registrar's satisfaction.
#ASSERT `the foreign exemption in section 14(1) applies` `an unregistered society wholly abroad with no local activity and the Registrar satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `the society is an unlawful society` `an unregistered society wholly abroad with no local activity and the Registrar satisfied`
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `the same, but the Registrar is not satisfied`
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `an unregistered society organised abroad that carries on an activity here`

-- Three more routes to the same status, each for a registered society.
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `a registered society's unapproved branch`
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `a registered society that uses a triad ritual`
#ASSERT `the society is an unlawful society` `a registered society after a dissolution order`

§ `The offences and their penalties`

#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `being or acting as a member of an unlawful society, or attending its meeting`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `knowingly allowing a meeting of an unlawful society on premises`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `inciting, inducing or inviting someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `using violence, threat or intimidation to induce someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 48
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `procuring a subscription or aid for an unlawful society`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `publishing, or possessing without lawful excuse, an unlawful society's documents`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `giving a copy of false rules with intent to mislead or defraud`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `possessing the books or insignia of a triad society`)'s `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`the penalty for the offence` `managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society`)'s `the maximum fine in dollars` EQUALS 10000

-- THE NON-BAILABLE LIST. The member's, the premises-owner's and the triad-possession offences are deemed
-- non-bailable and arrestable. The manager's offence, the most serious of the group at five years, is not.
#ASSERT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `being or acting as a member of an unlawful society, or attending its meeting`
#ASSERT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `knowingly allowing a meeting of an unlawful society on premises`
#ASSERT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `possessing the books or insignia of a triad society`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `managing or assisting in the management of an unlawful society`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `using violence, threat or intimidation to induce someone to join or help manage an unlawful society`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `procuring a subscription or aid for an unlawful society`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act deems the offence non-bailable and an arrestable case` `publishing, or possessing without lawful excuse, an unlawful society's documents`

§ `Fixtures -- conduct`

GIVEN `the society is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `manages` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attends` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `allows a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `incites` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses violence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `procures aid` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `publishes` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `possesses` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ConductFacts
DECIDE `conduct` `the society is unlawful` `manages` `is a member` `attends` `allows a meeting` `incites` `uses violence` `procures aid` `publishes` `possesses` `has an excuse` IS
    ConductFacts WITH
        `the society is an unlawful society` IS `the society is unlawful`
        `manages or assists in the management` IS `manages`
        `is or acts as a member` IS `is a member`
        `attends a meeting of the society` IS `attends`
        `knowingly allows a meeting on premises they own, occupy or control` IS `allows a meeting`
        `incites, induces or invites another to join or help manage` IS `incites`
        `uses violence, threat or intimidation to induce another to join or help manage` IS `uses violence`
        `procures or attempts to procure a subscription or aid` IS `procures aid`
        `prints, publishes, displays, sells, exposes for sale or posts its documents` IS `publishes`
        `has its documents in their possession` IS `possesses`
        `has lawful authority or excuse for the possession` IS `has an excuse`

`the committee chair of an unlawful society` MEANS `conduct` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a member who does nothing else` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`someone who attends one meeting and is not a member` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the manager of a lawful society` MEANS `conduct` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a landlord who knowingly lets the unlawful society meet in the hall` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a recruiter` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a recruiter who threatens` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a fundraiser` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a printer of the society's leaflets` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a printer with an excuse` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`someone who merely has a leaflet` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a researcher who has a leaflet for a lawful reason` MEANS `conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `Sections 14 to 18 -- the conduct`

#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 14(2)` `the committee chair of an unlawful society`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 14(3)` `the committee chair of an unlawful society`
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 14(3)` `a member who does nothing else`

-- Attendance is enough, with no membership and no knowledge stated.
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 14(3)` `someone who attends one meeting and is not a member`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 14(2)` `the manager of a lawful society`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 14(3)` `the manager of a lawful society`

#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 15(1)` `a landlord who knowingly lets the unlawful society meet in the hall`
#ASSERT `the person commits an offence in section 16` `a recruiter`
#ASSERT `the person commits an offence in section 16` `a recruiter who threatens`
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 17` `a fundraiser`
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 18` `a printer of the society's leaflets`

-- The lawful-excuse qualifier attaches to possession only.
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 18` `a printer with an excuse`
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 18` `someone who merely has a leaflet`
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 18` `a researcher who has a leaflet for a lawful reason`

§ `Sections 21 and 22 -- the presumptions`

#ASSERT `it is presumed to be a society consisting of 10 or more persons` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `it is presumed to be a society consisting of 10 or more persons` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the prosecution must prove the society has a name` TRUE

GIVEN `books` IS A BOOLEAN, `accounts` IS A BOOLEAN, `writings` IS A BOOLEAN, `seals` IS A BOOLEAN, `banners` IS A BOOLEAN, `insignia` IS A BOOLEAN, `lists of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Possession
DECIDE `found with` `books` `accounts` `writings` `seals` `banners` `insignia` `lists of members` IS
    Possession WITH
        `books` IS `books`
        `accounts` IS `accounts`
        `writings` IS `writings`
        `seals` IS `seals`
        `banners` IS `banners`
        `insignia` IS `insignia`
        `lists of members` IS `lists of members`

#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- The management presumption is drawn from books, accounts, lists of members and seals; not from writings,
-- banners or insignia.
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- THE ODDITY. A LIST OF MEMBERS alone raises the presumption of assisting in the management (five years) and not
-- the presumption of membership (three), although s 22(2) says "further".
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- The club treasurer's accounts book raises both.
#ASSERT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is presumed to assist in the management under section 22(2)` (`found with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is presumed a member under section 22(1)` (`found with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 23 -- triad rituals`

-- "Whether it is registered or not."
#ASSERT `the society is deemed unlawful by section 23(1)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the society is deemed unlawful by section 23(1)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the society is deemed unlawful by section 23(1)` TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 24 -- dissolution by the Minister`

GIVEN `unlawful or prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a certificate of the internal security Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fraud or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `incompatible with its objects and rules` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `inadequate rules not amended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `political rules not citizens only, not amended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `foreign connection not severed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wilful contravention` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `same name or symbol as a foreign organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DissolutionGrounds
DECIDE `grounds` `unlawful or prejudicial` `a certificate of the internal security Minister` `fraud or misrepresentation` `incompatible with its objects and rules` `inadequate rules not amended` `political rules not citizens only, not amended` `foreign connection not severed` `wilful contravention` `same name or symbol as a foreign organisation` IS
    DissolutionGrounds WITH
        `it appears the society is used for unlawful purposes, or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order, or against national security or interest` IS `unlawful or prejudicial`
        `a certificate of the internal security Minister states the society is used for purposes against national security` IS `a certificate of the internal security Minister`
        `it appears registration was procured by fraud or misrepresentation` IS `fraud or misrepresentation`
        `it appears the society is used for purposes incompatible with its objects and rules` IS `incompatible with its objects and rules`
        `its rules are inadequate and it failed without reasonable cause to amend them within 3 months of a direction` IS `inadequate rules not amended`
        `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens and it failed without reasonable cause to amend within 3 months of a direction` IS `political rules not citizens only, not amended`
        `it is a political association with a foreign connection and failed to satisfy the Registrar it severed it within 3 months of a direction` IS `foreign connection not severed`
        `it appears the society wilfully contravened the Act, the regulations or its own rules` IS `wilful contravention`
        `it is a political association using the same name or symbol as an organisation outside Singapore` IS `same name or symbol as a foreign organisation`

#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Limb (g): a breach of the society's OWN RULES is a ground.
#ASSERT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- The internal security Minister's certificate is conclusive of limb (a).
#ASSERT `the ground in section 24(1)(a) is made out` (`grounds` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 24(6): the same name or symbol is sufficient evidence of a connection, but limb (f) also needs a failure
-- to sever it within three months of a direction, so the name alone dissolves nothing.
#ASSERT `the foreign connection in limb (f) is established by the name or symbol alone` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may order the society dissolved` (`grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- No appeal or review.
#ASSERT NOT `the Act provides an appeal or review against an order under section 24`

GIVEN `was an officer on the date of the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since the order` IS A NUMBER, `permission given` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting as an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN IneligibilityFacts
DECIDE `a former officer` `was an officer on the date of the order` `years since the order` `permission given` `acting as an officer` IS
    IneligibilityFacts WITH
        `was an officer of the society on the date of the dissolution order` IS `was an officer on the date of the order`
        `years since the order` IS `years since the order`
        `the Minister gave written permission` IS `permission given`
        `is acting or elected as an officer of another society` IS `acting as an officer`

#ASSERT `the person is ineligible under section 24(4)` (`a former officer` TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 24(5)` (`a former officer` TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE)

-- Three years, from the date of the order.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is ineligible under section 24(4)` (`a former officer` TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 24(5)` (`a former officer` TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 24(5)` (`a former officer` TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 24(5)` (`a former officer` TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is ineligible under section 24(4)` (`a former officer` FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE)

§ `Section 25 -- the property`

#ASSERT `the surplus goes to the Consolidated Fund` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the surplus goes to the members according to the rules` TRUE
#ASSERT `the surplus goes to the members according to the rules` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the surplus goes to the Consolidated Fund` FALSE

-- It vests forthwith; no court order is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `the society's property vests in the Official Receiver or the appointed officer only after a court order`
